# Force LF everywhere, regardless of a contributor's local Git config.
#
# Without this, a Windows machine with the common `core.autocrlf=true` default
# checks out every tracked file as CRLF. The mixed-line-ending pre-commit hook
# (--fix=lf) then rewrites nearly the whole tree the moment `make setup` /
# the first commit runs `pre-commit run --all-files` — a surprise mass-diff
# on day one that has nothing to do with whatever the contributor actually
# changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch line endings, and don't diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# uv.lock is generated and large (hundreds of hashed entries). Marking it keeps it
# collapsed in GitHub diffs and out of `git diff` by default, so a weekly
# Dependabot bump stays reviewable instead of burying the pyproject.toml change
# it accompanies. It is still tracked, still committed, still diffable with
# `git diff -- uv.lock`.
uv.lock -diff linguist-generated=true
